Agentic AI Unleashed: AWS & NVIDIA Hackathon: Build the future of agentic AI with AWS and NVIDIA - Devpost Agentic AI Unleashed: AWS & NVIDIA Hackathon Build the future of agentic AI with AWS and NVIDIA This hackathon has ended Find more hackathons View the winners Who can participate Above legal age of majority in country of residence Specific countries/territories excluded × Specific countries/territories excluded Argentina Australia Brazil Crimea Cuba France Germany Hong Kong Indonesia Iran Islamic Republic of Italy Korea Democratic People's Republic of Malaysia Philippines Poland Quebec Russia Singapore Spain Thailand United Arab Emirates Vietnam No countries/territories match your search. View full rules View schedule Oct 13 – Nov 4, 2025 Online Public 4 non-cash prizes 1955 participants AWS & NVIDIA Managed by Devpost Enterprise DevOps Machine Learning/AI About the challenge Are you ready to push the boundaries of AI? Build the next generation of intelligent, autonomous applications. This isn't just a hackathon—it's your chance to unleash the power of Agentic AI and show the world what's possible. Your challenge is to create an Agentic Application—using the llama-3 1-nemotron-nano-8B-v1 large language reasoning mode, deployed as an NVIDIA NIM inference microservice, and at least one Retrieval Embedding NIM . Your project will be deployed on the scalable infrastructure of either an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) Cluster or an Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint. It's a full-stack AI project that will test your skills and leave you with a real-world application. Why Participate? This hackathon is more than just a competition, it's a launchpad for your skills and creativity. Level Up Your Skills: Get hands-on experience with cutting-edge AI models and AWS services. This is your chance to build a real-world project that will supercharge your portfolio. Connect with Experts: Network with fellow developers, learn from industry leaders, and get help from team experts at AWS and NVIDIA. Win Big: Compete for recognition and premium prizes. Get started: Access & Credits We want to make it easy for you to focus on the fun part—building! Teams of enterprise professionals may request $100 USD in Promotional Credits to help you complete your project. Here’s how to get them: Make sure your team is registered for the hackathon. Have a valid submission idea ready to go. Complete this form . Credits will be distributed to each team. *Note: The $100 promotional credit is a one-time voucher per team/project and is not cumulative or transferable. Once an individual has been part of a team that has received a credit, they are ineligible to receive another credit, even if they join a different team or start a new project. We've set aside these credits to help you get started, but keep a couple of important things in mind: The $100 promotional credits can cover approximately 24 hours of the two required NVIDIA NIM microservices running on either SageMaker or Amazon EKS. Your dashboard will show your remaining balance, and you will be responsible for the allocation of this budget to the overall AWS services you will need, i.e. NVIDIA NIM microservices running on either Amazon SageMaker AI or Amazon EKS, storage, networking, security services etc. Be sure to monitor your usage dashboard to avoid running out of credit before the hackathon ends. Once all credits are exhausted, your access to the services will be cut off, and no further usage will be allowed, so keep an eye on your dashboard to monitor your remaining balance. In the meantime, get to know the NVIDIA and AWS resources! Interact, and experiment with the NVIDIA NIM microservices hosted on build.nvidia.com . In addition, AWS offers AWS Free Tier , where you can gain hands-on experience with AWS products and services. Are you ready to take on the challenge? Requirements What to Create Build an Agentic Application that uses the llama-3 1-nemotron-nano-8B-v1 large language reasoning mode, deployed as an NVIDIA NIM inference microservice, and at least one Retrieval Embedding NIM , all deployed on either an Amazon EKS Cluster or an Amazon SageMaker AI endpoint. What to Submit Text description that explains the features and functionality of your project Demo video (should be under three minutes) URL to your public code repository README file that contains deployment instructions Please check the official Rules page for full details. Hackathon Sponsors Prizes 4 non-cash prizes Grand Prize 1 winner • NVIDIA GPU: PNY - RTX 6000 ADA (approximate value $6,900) • Promotion on NVIDIA developer social channels • Swag • 1,000 Brev.dev credits • Credits for NVIDIA's DLI platform for training and certification Second Place 1 winner • NVIDIA GPU: MSI - RTX 5090 32G (approximate value $2,500) • Promotion on NVIDIA developer social channels • Swag • 500 Brev.dev credits • Credits for NVIDIA's DLI platform for training and certification Third Place 1 winner • NVIDIA GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Founders Edition (approximate value $1,250) • Promotion on NVIDIA developer social channels • Swag • 300 Brev.dev credits • Credits for NVIDIA's DLI platform for training and certification Most Valuable Participant 1 winner • NVIDIA GPU: MSI - RTX 5090 32G (approximate value $2,500) • Promotion on NVIDIA developer social channels • Swag • Credits for NVIDIA's DLI platform for training and certification Devpost Achievements Submitting to this hackathon could earn you: Judges Julie Tang Principal Partner Marketing Manager, ISV | Amazon Web Services Brian Kreitzer Senior Partner Solutions Architect | Amazon Web Services Avichal Chum Senior Solutions Architect | Amazon Web Services Chris Smith Senior WW Specialist SA, GenAI | Amazon Web Services Curtice Lockhart Senior Solutions Architect | NVIDIA Jay Rodge Senior Developer Advocate | NVIDIA Abhinav Balasubramanian Senior Software Engineer | NVIDIA Dimitri Maltezakis Vathypetrou Cloud Developer Relations | NVIDIA Judging Criteria Technological Implementation Does the interaction with NVIDIA and AWS demonstrate quality software development? Design Is the user experience and design of the project well thought out? Potential Impact How big of an impact could the project have on the target audience? Quality of the Idea How creative and unique is the project? Questions? Email the hackathon manager Tell your friends Hackathon sponsors This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.
