NemoClaw NVIDIA x ASUS Hackathon @ UCSC: 24 Hours of Hacking. 40 DGX Sparks. Build the Future. - Devpost NemoClaw NVIDIA x ASUS Hackathon @ UCSC NemoClaw NVIDIA x ASUS Hackathon @ UCSC 24 Hours of Hacking. 40 DGX Sparks. Build the Future. This hackathon has ended Find more hackathons View the winners Who can participate Anyone accepted into the event Above legal age of majority in country of residence Team required US only View full rules View schedule May 16, 2026 University of California, Santa Cruz Invite only 4 non-cash prizes 209 participants NVIDIA Machine Learning/AI Open Ended Robotic Process Automation ​About the Event ​Autonomous AI agents are running on laptops, connecting to real tools, and completing real tasks. Now it's your turn to build one. ​In this 24-hour hackathon hosted by NVIDIA, your challenge is to build a working autonomous agent application using OpenClaw and NVIDIA Nemotron models. We want agents that take action, handle live data, and execute complex multi-step workflows. The use case is yours to define. ​The Deliverable ​Your submission needs to be a deployed, working OpenClaw agent powered by Nemotron that autonomously handles a task with persistent memory, multi-step reasoning, and live tool use. Not a prototype. Not a pitch deck. Something that runs. Choose Your Compute Path ​On-device: Build locally on ASUS Ascent GX10 (DGX Spark). ​Cloud: Build via fully sponsored compute instances on NVIDIA Brev. ​The Three Prize Tracks ​Cloud Track: Brev-driven project for OpenClaw and NVIDIA Nemotron Models. ​Edge Track: ASUS Ascent GX10-driven project for OpenClaw and NVIDIA Nemotron Models. ​Bonus Track (Best Use of NemoClaw): Want to go further? Deploy your agent using NVIDIA NemoClaw for an additional prize category. NemoClaw wraps your OpenClaw agent in a hardened sandbox with policy-based security and privacy guardrails, running Nemotron locally on-device. Teams that deploy via NemoClaw and demonstrate its security controls will be judged separately for this track. (Note: NemoClaw is currently in early preview so some rough edges are expected). BONUS Hack.dev Track (Best Use Case for UCSC): Identify an issue at UC Santa Cruz and come up with an impactful and innovative solution for students. ​The Details ​Who: Open to UC Santa Cruz students of all experience levels. No prior OpenClaw experience required. A getting-started guide will be shared before the event. You can work in teams of 1-4. ​Food: Fully catered for 24 hours. Energy, caffeine, and meals are on us. ​Title Sponsors: NVIDIA, ASUS, Baskin School of Engineering. ​Prizes: ​The ASUS Ascent (DGX Spark) (Valued at $4000) ​Jetson Nano Orins ​Exclusive Premium NVIDIA Swag ​High-Value Brev.dev Compute Credits ​Career Fast-Tracking: Direct portfolio reviews and internship pipeline opportunities with NVIDIA Hiring Managers Requirements What to Build Think outside the box. Design an intuitive and polished user interface, build a secure and scalable backend, and craft a compelling marketing strategy that makes the product stand out. Most importantly, emphasize the unique, innovative use of our hackathon's unique tech tools in your launched product. What to Submit Your submission needs to be a deployed, working OpenClaw agent powered by Nemotron that autonomously handles a task with persistent memory, multi-step reasoning, and live tool use. Not a prototype. Not a pitch deck. Something that runs. Hackathon Sponsors Prizes 4 non-cash prizes Best Use of DGX Spark 1 winner 4 Jetson Orin Nanos($250 each), Nvidia Exclusive Swag and Merch, ASUS ASCENT GX10($4000), Brev Credits Best Use of Brev 1 winner 4 Jetson Orin Nanos, Nvidia Exclusive Swag and Merch, Brev Credits Best Use of NemoClaw 1 winner 4 Jetson Orin Nanos, Nvidia Exclusive Swag and Merch, Brev Credits Best for UCSC 1 winner Airpod 4s for each team member Devpost Achievements Submitting to this hackathon could earn you: Judges Abhinav Balasubramanian NVIDIA Judging Criteria Creativity The project's originality and innovative problem-solving approach in addressing a challenge Functionality The projects functional prototype, live demonstration of effectiveness and stability, ensuring meaningful integration of tech stack. Scope of Completion The project's completeness, polish, and user experience, ensuring a seamless and well-structured workflow. Presentation Clear, engaging, and well-structured presentation that effectively communicates the project core use case, technical depth, and business impact to diverse audiences. Use of NVIDIA tools A team's effective, impactful, and innovative integration of NVIDIA NIM, SDKs, libraries, and tools to enhance their projects. With the additional use of Nemo Claw/Open Claw, if applying for the Nemo Claw track. Use of NVIDIA Nematron Models The team's effective, impactful, and innovative integration of NVIDIA's Nemotron models to enable sophisticated reasoning and agentic capabilities within their project. Use of Brev The team's effective, impactful, and innovative integration of NVIDIA Brev.dev to enable sophisticated reasoning and heavy capabilities with their projects Questions? Email the hackathon manager Tell your friends Hackathon sponsors This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.
