l tools The challenges of integrating qualitative data into quantitative models How We Built It We built R.E.A.L.M. using a stack that includes: Streamlit for the frontend, ensuring a responsive and intuitive user interface Python  for the backend, handling complex calculations and data processing Perplexity API exploring the internet SQLite for storage The core of R.E.A.L.M. is our innovative scoring system that digitizes the 5C approach: Character : AI-driven analysis of the project management team's track record Capacity : Automated assessment of project feasibility and timeline Capital : Real-time financial modeling and stress testing Collateral : Smart evaluation of project assets and guarantees Conditions : AI-powered analysis of market conditions and external factors Challenges We Faced Our journey wasn't without obstacles: User Experience : Balancing comprehensive analysis with user-friendliness was tricky. To refine our interface, we conducted multiple user testing sessions. Processing Time : A technical hurdle was ensuring quick response times while processing complex risk calculations. To address this, we optimized our backend and implemented efficient caching mechanisms. Despite these challenges, R.E.A.L.M. emerged as a powerful tool that will transform project-based facultative reinsurance assessment, making it faster, more accurate, and more accessible to underwriters worldwide. Built With langchain openai perplexity python streamlit Submitted to HackAI - Dell and NVIDIA Challenge Winner Honorable Mention Created by Draft the idea and develop the engine Ekki Rinaldi 7 years in AI and Blockchain billysutomo Like 2 2 people like this: Share this project: Updates Ekki Rinaldi started this project — Oct 02, 2024 01:49 AM EDT Leave feedback 

